== Tofu Pancetta ==

Whisk together @vegan mayo{2%tbsp}, @soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @liquid smoke{1%tsp}, @sriracha{1%tbsp}, @vegan worcestershire{1%tbsp}, @nutritional yeast{1%tbsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @onion powder{1%tsp}, @smoked paprika{2%tsp}, @salt{to taste}. I recommend blending in a small bullet style blender if possible to fully emulsify it, but whisking will work too.

Pat @super firm tofu{8%oz} dry, then dice it into small cubes (about 1/4" thick).

Heat up a #non-stick pan{} or well-seasoned pan over medium heat with @cooking oil{1-2%tbsp}. Add the cubed tofu, toss to coat in the oil, then let them sit undisturbed for ~{2-3%minutes}. Toss them again, and repeat this process until they are browned to your liking.

Lower the heat to medium low, and pour over the sauce. Stir to coat. Cook until the sauce has been absorbed. Stir frequently to avoid burning, and lower the heat more if you notice any black bits forming. Once cooked to your liking, remove from the pan and reserve.


== Carbonara ==

Cook @spaghetti{8-12%oz} according to package instructions. Use 8oz for a very saucy pasta, or up to 12oz for less saucy. I cook 10oz for this recipe and find that to be perfect.

While the pasta cooks, blend up all the ingredients for the Carbonara sauce: @vegan mayo{1/4%cup}, @silken tofu{3/4%cup}(or @cashew cream{}), @unsweetened plant milk{1/2%cup}, @nutritional yeast{2%tbsp}, @vegan parmesan{1/4%cup}(or more @nutritional yeast{}), @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, @miso paste{1%tsp}, @dijon mustard{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, @onion powder{1/4%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1/4%tsp}, @turmeric{1/4%tsp}, and @salt{to taste}. 

Add the sauce to a pan and heat over medium low. Once the pasta is cooked, reserve about 1 cup of the pasta water. Add the cooked spaghetti to the sauce and stir to coat. If the sauce feels too thick, add a bit of the reserved pasta water to loosen it up and make it creamier too! Start with about @pasta water{1/4%cup} or less and add as needed.

Season with anything you like! @salt{} and @ground black pepper{}, @black salt{dash}(for an eggy flavor), more @vegan parmesan{}, or fresh herbs like basil or parsley.

> Important Note: I don't recommend mixing the Tofu Pancetta directly into the Sauce or Pasta. I find that the marinade will sometimes come loose from the tofu once heated and will disperse into the sauce which makes it too salty. It's best to top the finished pasta with it on each plate so you get nice little salty isolated bits instead!

> I highly recommend using Super Firm Tofu which is vacuum packed with very little water for the Tofu Pancetta. You can try using Extra Firm, but you'll want to press it for at least ~{30%minutes} and it may not crisp up as much.
